# Byte-exact checkouts.
#
# SHA256SUMS and inventory.json are computed over exact file bytes, so a
# checkout has to reproduce those bytes on every platform. By default Git
# rewrites LF -> CRLF in text files when core.autocrlf is on (the Windows
# default), which changes every hash: a Windows clone currently fails the
# integrity check on ~2,300 files while the committed content is correct.
#
# "-text" disables all line-ending conversion, so what is committed is what
# is checked out, everywhere.
* -text

*.pdf binary
